BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sparrows (1926)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T150000
DTSTAMP:20260729T034639Z
UID:occ-942@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Mary Pickford's 1926 silent classic with live theatre organ ac
 companiment and an organ pops pre-show.\n\nMary Pickford's 1926 silent cla
 ssic. Pickford plays Molly\, oldest of a brood of orphans held on a baby f
 arm in the middle of an alligator swamp\; when their cruel keeper decides 
 one child must be gotten rid of\, she leads the escape across the bog. Hou
 se organist Ron Carter accompanies live on the Mighty Allen theatre organ\
 , a digital recreation of a 1920s Wurlitzer whose toy counter supplies whi
 stles\, gunshots\, and thunder. Part of the Strand's Silent Film Series\, 
 with an organ pops concert starting a half hour before the film. Runs 1 ho
 ur 49 minutes.
GEO:33.9536122;-84.5492054
LAST-MODIFIED:20260728T204247Z
LOCATION:The Strand Theatre\, 117 N Park Square
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://thestrand.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/instances/a0FPs0000
 06X9ttMAC
END:VEVENT
